# Cell from playpick: mode=walk, boss=skyward (coverage label only --
# evening steers at no boss, the walk starts at the door same as any
# other), spec=shaman:restoration, style=dodge, size=25, difficulty=heroic,
# view=820x1180,touch, save=carried (behaves as fresh per #273 -- the
# dev-server port is pid-derived so localStorage never actually carries
# across separate playbot invocations, so #b=marrow&s=25&h=1 is used to
# unlock the chain up to 25-heroic the same way every other "carried at
# heroic" cell in this job has).
#
# Checked sessions.jsonl and direction.md first. shaman:restoration has
# been played under good, auto, flee, mash and melee before, but never
# under dodge -- and dodge has never been given to a healer spec on this
# boss at all (its two healer readings so far, priest:discipline/dodge and
# priest:discipline/good, were both on skyward via mode=daily, not a
# walked evening). dodge never presses an ability (scripts/playbot.ts:929,
# the `acting === 'dodge' || acting === 'good'` branch only steers; the
# press loop below it is gated on styles that are not dodge), so this is
# the clearest test yet of whether a 25-heroic evening can survive THE
# VIGIL and The Bonegrinder with its one healer slot pressing nothing at
# all for the whole walk -- extending hypothesis 1 (idle/dodge-shaped
# styles winning without cost) from single boss rooms to a full evening
# with a healer specifically, which no session has run before.
open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
tap next
tap class:shaman:restoration
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start

evening dodge 260 6
state
shot after-evening
says
bill
